{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning",
    "title": "Treatment Planning",
    "order": 13
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning-thorax",
    "title": "Thorax Treatment Planning",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Two Central Challenges \u2014 Motion and Heterogeneity",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Thoracic planning is defined by "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "two",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " problems working at once, which is what sets it apart from most other sites:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "bulletList",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Respiratory motion.",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " Lung and mediastinal tumors travel with every breath. Lower-lobe lesions near the diaphragm can move well over a centimeter, so a single planning snapshot does not tell you where the target actually spends its time."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "listItem",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "paragraph",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "Tissue heterogeneity.",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " The beam crosses low-density lung on its way to the target. The treatment planning system "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "must",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "italic"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " apply "
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": "heterogeneity (density) correction",
                              "marks": [
                                {
                                  "type": "bold"
                                }
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "type": "text",
                              "text": " \u2014 calculating dose as if the chest were uniform water overestimates tumor dose and misrepresents the penumbra at the tumor\u2013lung interface."
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Layered on top of both is the crowd of critical structures packed into a small volume: heart, esophagus, spinal cord, and the uninvolved lung itself."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Positioning and Motion Management",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Common setup: "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "supine, both arms raised above the head",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " on a wingboard or T-bar grips (clearing the lateral and oblique beam paths), immobilized on a chest board or vac-lok cushion for day-to-day reproducibility."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "4D-CT",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " characterizes the tumor's motion envelope across the breathing cycle so an "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "ITV (Internal Target Volume)",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " can be built directly from where the target actually travels. Motion can also be reduced rather than just measured: "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "deep inspiration breath-hold (DIBH)",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " holds the target still and pushes the heart away from the chest wall, "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "respiratory gating",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " treats only during a chosen phase, and "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "abdominal compression",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " limits diaphragm excursion."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page2_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Beyond holding the target still, what added benefit makes deep inspiration breath-hold (DIBH) especially attractive for many thoracic and left-sided cases?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "It inflates the lungs and displaces the heart, lowering dose to the heart and normal lung",
              "It removes the need for heterogeneity correction in the plan"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "On inspiration the expanded lung pushes the heart inferiorly and away from the chest wall, so DIBH both freezes motion and physically moves critical structures out of the high-dose region. Heterogeneity correction is a dose-calculation step and is still required regardless of breathing technique."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Target Volumes",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Thoracic targets follow the standard GTV/CTV/ITV/PTV hierarchy, with contouring nuances specific to the chest:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Volume"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Thorax-specific consideration"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "GTV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Contoured using "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "both windows",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": ": the "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "lung window",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "italic"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " for the parenchymal tumor edge and the "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "mediastinal (soft-tissue) window",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "italic"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " for nodal and mediastinal extension. PET/CT fusion further clarifies active disease from atelectasis"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "CTV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "GTV plus a margin for microscopic spread, edited off anatomic barriers the tumor cannot cross (chest wall, intact bone, major vessels)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "ITV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "CTV expanded to cover the respiratory motion measured on 4D-CT \u2014 "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "lower-lobe tumors require a larger ITV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " than upper-lobe tumors because they move more with the diaphragm"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "PTV",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "ITV plus a setup-uncertainty margin. As with any moving-target site, ITV sits "
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "between",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "italic"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": " CTV and PTV in the expansion sequence"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Why is the GTV contoured on both lung and mediastinal windows?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "The lung window shows the parenchymal tumor extent while the mediastinal window shows soft-tissue and nodal extension; using both avoids under- or over-contouring",
              "The mediastinal window is only used to check bone detail of the ribs and vertebrae"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Each window reveals a different tissue interface \u2014 the parenchymal edge is clearest on lung window, soft-tissue and nodal disease on mediastinal window. Relying on one alone systematically mis-sizes the GTV."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Organ-at-Risk Constraints",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Structure"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Constraint (typical conventional fractionation, ~60 Gy)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Lungs (both, minus GTV)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "V20 \u2264 30\u201335%; Mean Lung Dose \u2264 20 Gy (lower is better \u2014 drives radiation pneumonitis risk)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Heart"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Mean \u2264 26 Gy; V30 \u2264 46%; minimize high-dose volume"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Esophagus"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Mean \u2264 34 Gy; limit high-dose length to reduce acute esophagitis"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Spinal cord"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Max \u2264 45\u201350 Gy"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Brachial plexus"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "\u2264 60\u201366 Gy \u2014 specifically relevant for apical / superior sulcus (Pancoast) tumors"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "SBRT for early-stage peripheral disease uses far tighter, ablative constraints given the very high dose per fraction \u2014 a genuinely different planning problem from conventional fractionation, with particular caution near the central \"no-fly zone\" around the proximal bronchial tree."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Techniques and Typical Dose",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "ARRT explicitly distinguishes two thoracic treatment categories, and it is worth understanding why each is chosen:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Multi-field (non-IMRT) 3D-CRT"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Classic approach using a handful of shaped static fields \u2014 for example, AP/PA fields to roughly 40\u201345 Gy, then "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "off-cord oblique fields",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " to boost the target while dropping the spinal cord out of the high-dose beam. Field shapes are drawn in beam's-eye-view with the MLC."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "IMRT / Volumetric Arc Therapy (VMAT)"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Modulated delivery gives better conformality around concave targets and tighter sparing when heart, cord, and esophagus crowd the target. The tradeoff is a larger "
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "low-dose bath",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " (high V5) spread across normal lung, which can itself raise pneumonitis risk \u2014 so the \"more modulation\" choice is not automatically the safer one in the chest."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Typical dose:",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " definitive NSCLC is commonly "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "60\u201366 Gy in 30\u201333 fractions",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " (2 Gy/fx), frequently with concurrent chemotherapy. "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "SBRT",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": " for early-stage, medically inoperable peripheral tumors is commonly "
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "48\u201354 Gy in 3\u20135 fractions",
                          "marks": [
                            {
                              "type": "bold"
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": ", with risk-adapted fractionation (e.g., 50 Gy in 5) for central lesions."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page5_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "What is the main tradeoff of choosing IMRT/VMAT over multi-field 3D-CRT in the thorax?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Better conformality and OAR sparing, but a larger low-dose bath (high V5) to normal lung",
              "It delivers a more uniform dose but can no longer account for tissue heterogeneity"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Modulation buys conformality and sparing of crowded OARs at the cost of spreading low dose more widely through healthy lung, which matters for pneumonitis risk. Heterogeneity correction applies to both techniques."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Wrap-Up",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered the two defining thoracic challenges (respiratory motion and tissue heterogeneity), positioning with 4D-CT/ITV and DIBH/gating, the both-windows approach to GTV contouring and the upper- vs. lower-lobe motion difference, the key OAR constraints, and the ARRT distinction between multi-field 3D-CRT and IMRT/VMAT with typical dose ranges."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
